//! task: translate
//! ask: Translate this C to Exsecutor.
//!   ```c
//!   int in_range(uint32_t x, uint32_t lo, uint32_t hi) {
//!       return x >= lo && x <= hi;
//!   }
//!   ```
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §8.4, §8.6
//! explain: `>=` and `<=` are the words `ge` and `le`, and `&&` is the short-circuit `et`. There is no boolean expression type to return directly, so the condition selects between the one-bit values 1 and 0 of `u1`.

publica functio intra(x: u32, lo: u32, hi: u32) -> u1 {
    si x ge lo et x le hi {
        redde 1;
    }
    redde 0;
}
